cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OSCA: Origin, Semantic, and Consequence Authority"
message: "If you use this research or implementation, please cite as below."
type: software
version: "0.1.0-research-draft"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
abstract: |
  OSCA (Origin, Semantic, and Consequence Authority) is a multi-tier
  authorization architecture for autonomous AI agents. It separates
  authority into three independently verifiable tiers — origin, semantic,
  and consequence — and binds them atomically at execution time. Every
  authorized action carries an auditable decision trace from origin
  through consequence.

  The project spans six intersecting research domains: computer science
  and software engineering, applied mathematics and numerical computing,
  cybersecurity and systems theory, computational physics, quantum
  computing, and artificial intelligence and autonomous systems.

  No empirical data has been collected at the time of this release.
